===Verb===
{{en-verb|stand<,,stood> down}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} To [[wait]]; to stop [[pursuing]], stop [[fighting]], or relax from a heightened [[readiness]] posture.
#: {{ant|en|square off|square up}}
#: {{ux|en|They ordered the troops to '''stand down''' for the moment.}}
# {{lb|en|ambitransitive}} To [[withdraw]] or [[retire]] from a [[position]] or from a team.
#: {{syn|en|stand aside|step down}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2023 November 29|title=Last remaining DB Cargo Class 60s face final workings in December|journal=RAIL|issue=997|page=19|text=The remaining four locomotives in traffic {{...}} are all expected to be '''stood down''' due to their high engine hours, as well as being due exams which the company is not prepared to undertake.}}